    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: Across animal population time series, compare variance and density dependence attributable to prey resources versus predator abundance using lagged causal models or removals. More populations primarily limited by predation would support 'very frequently.'";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.1.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "Food and predator time series rarely accompany focal abundance.", "Top-down and bottom-up effects interact and share climate drivers.";
